      "alignment": "neutral",
      "cr": 1,
      "type": {
        "value": "humanoid",
        "subtype": "time scholar"
      },
      "biography": {
        "value": "<h2>Oswald Pendlewick — The Borrower of Time</h2><p>Ordinary human archivist, modest spellcaster, nervous and physically fragile. His spectacular time powers come solely from the hidden Hourglass of Unfinished Moments, tied to the Avatar of Time.</p><h3>GM-only: The Price of Time</h3><p>Unlimited artifact uses, but each incurs Temporal Strain. 3+: half walking speed. Reaching 6: disadvantage on attacks/checks and 1d4 years lost. Reaching 9: 1d6 more years lost. Each use at 9+: 2d6 HP loss, Constitution save DC 10 + strain above 9 or unconsciousness; each subsequent use also loses 1d6 years. Long rest recovers 3 strain, never years. Ordinary arcane spells never increase strain.</p><p>Oswald uses rewinds for theft, indulgence and undoing his mistakes; he can anchor chosen small changes. Captain Varrin is after the artifact on Marsh Toreg's behalf. GM resolves effects that change timeline manually. Use the Oswald — Hourglass Controls macro or on-sheet activities.</p>"
      }
    },
    "traits": {
      "size": "med",
      "languages": {
        "value": [
          "common"
        ],
        "custom": "Elvish and several dead scholarly dialects"
      }
    }
  },
